</div><includeonly>{{#if:{{{1|}}}||[[Category:Notes with no text]]}}</includeonly></onlyinclude><!--
  The category is how a note with no text says so. Without it the placeholder above draws, the
  page builds, and nothing else says anything: an unnamed argument holding "=" or "|" is parsed
  as a named one, so {{note|a=b}} reaches {{{1}}} with nothing. Write that one {{note|1=a=b}}.

  WikvenFailOnCategories in .wikven.yaml names the category, so a build that fills it stops and
  says which page did. includeonly keeps this page itself out of it; it is outside onlyinclude
  so that no page carries it.
-->
